.s-fpic.s-fpic-v1 { background: var(--ta); }
.s-fpic-v1 span, .s-fpic-v1::before { color: var(--tb); }
.s-fpic.s-fpic-v2 { justify-content: center; align-items: center; text-align: center; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ta) 30%, var(--tb)); }
.s-fpic-v2 span { color: #F7F1E6; }
.s-fpic-v2::before { inset-inline: 0; text-align: center; }
/* In a song's card it leads, the card's full width over its number and title. */
/* The song card's head: its title is the feature, set large over its picture (Hillel, 2026-11-18: "Lets make the phots
   more of a background element and the song titke the feature"; then "Photos too dark", "All cards look alike": "maybe
   let some of the color through"). The picture fills the head in its own colours; a gradient only where the title sits,
   dark at the foot and leaning to the page's palette (--tb), clear by the top half, gives the cream title its AA, with a
